cover all the requirements of the PRD\\n5. **Validate Test Compliance**: Ensure all tests comply with testing requirements\\n\\n## Validation Criteria\\n\\n### Test Fidelity\\n- Every success criterion in the PRD has at least one spec\\n- Edge cases are covered (nil, empty strings, invalid inputs)\\n- Error cases are tested\\n- Key behaviors are tested, not just happy paths\\n\\n### Test Quality\\n- Test names describe BEHAVIOR, not implementation\\n - Good: \\\"it returns user when credentials are valid\\\"\\n - Bad: \\\"it calls authenticate method\\\"\\n- Tests use proper RSpec structure (describe/context/it)\\n- No hardcoded values that obscure intent\\n- Assertions are specific and meaningful\\n\\n### Test Compliance\\n- Specs focus on outputs and behaviors, not internal implementation\\n- Tests are isolated (no dependencies on order)\\n- Follow patterns from TESTING.md if applicable\\n\\nWhen evaluating, ask yourself:\\n\\n- do these specs accurately reflect what's required by the PRD?\\n- am I testing the right things - outputs & behaviours, not implementation?\\n- am I testing the right areas - unit tests for isolated behaviour?\\n\\n## Return Format\\n\\nReturn \\\"SUCCESS: {short summary}\\\" if:\\n- All PRD criteria are covered\\n- Specs follow quality standards\\n- No missing edge cases or error cases\\n\\nReturn \\\"FAILURE: {failure reason}\\\" if any issues are found.\\n\\nBe SPECIFIC in your feedback:\\n- What PRD requirement is missing?\\n- Which test names are poorly written?\\n- What edge cases are untested?\\n- What TESTING.md standard is violated?\\n\\n## Important\\n\\n- Read SPECS only, not implementation code\\n- Focus on WHAT should be tested, not HOW\\n- If specs are minimal but technically correct, still reject if they miss obvious edge cases\\n\\n## Return Content\\n\\nOn SUCCESS: provide a short summary if:\\n- All PRD criteria are covered\\n- Specs follow quality standards\\n- No missing edge cases or error cases\\n\\nOn FAILURE: provide specific details if any issues are found:\\n- What PRD requirement is missing?\\n- Which test names are poorly written?\\n- What edge cases are untested?\\n- What TESTING.md standard is violated?\",\"file_path\":\"/Users/davekinkead/Projects/son-of-ralph/agents/REVIEWER.md\",\"success\":true}","tool_call_id":"call_-7965122985345375327"},{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"file_path\":\"/Users/davekinkead/Projects/son-of-ralph/agents/REVIEWER.md\",\"old_string\":\"- do these specs accurately reflect what's required by the PRD?\\n- am I testing the right things - outputs & behaviours, not implementation?\\n- am I testing the right areas - unit tests for isolated behaviour?\\n\\n## Return Format\\n\\nReturn \\\"SUCCESS: {short summary}\\\" if:\\n- All PRD criteria are covered\\n- Specs follow quality standards\\n- No missing edge cases or error cases\\n\\nReturn \\\"FAILURE: {failure reason}\\\" if any issues are found.\\n\\nBe SPECIFIC in your feedback:\\n- What PRD requirement is missing?\\n- Which test names are poorly written?\\n- What edge cases are untested?\\n- What TESTING.md standard is violated?\\n\\n## Important\",\"new_string\":\"- do these specs accurately reflect what's required by the PRD?\\n- am I testing the right things - outputs & behaviours, not implementation?\\n- am I testing the right areas - unit tests for isolated behaviour?\\n\\n## Important\"}","name":"editfile"},"id":"call_-7965175899344374442","index":0,"type":"function"}]},{"role":"tool","content":"{\"success\":true,\"file_path\":\"/Users/davekinkead/Projects/son-of-ralph/agents/REVIEWER.md\"}","tool_call_id":"call_-7965175899344374442"},{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"file_path\":\"/Users/davekinkead/Projects/son-of-ralph/agents/REVIEWER.md\",\"old_string\":\"## Important\\n\\n- Read SPECS only, not implementation code\\n- Focus on WHAT should be tested, not HOW\\n- If specs are minimal but technically correct, still reject if they miss obvious edge cases\\n\\n## Return Content\\n\\nOn SUCCESS: provide a short summary if:\\n- All PRD criteria are covered\\n- Specs follow quality standards\\n- No missing edge cases or error cases\\n\\nOn FAILURE: provide specific details if any issues are found:\\n- What PRD requirement is missing?\\n- Which test names are poorly written?\\n- What edge cases are untested?\\n- What TESTING.md standard is violated?\",\"new_string\":\"## Important\\n\\n- Read SPECS only, not implementation code\\n- Focus on WHAT should be tested, not HOW\\n- If specs are minimal but technically correct, still reject if they miss obvious edge cases\\n\\nOn SUCCESS: provide a short summary if all PRD criteria are covered, specs follow quality standards, and no missing edge cases or error cases.\\n\\nOn FAILURE: provide specific details if any issues are found:\\n- What PRD requirement is missing?\\n- Which test names are poorly written?\\n- What edge cases are untested?\\n- What TESTING.md standard is violated?\"}","name":"editfile"},"id":"call_-7965096665784976247","index":0,"type":"function"}]},{"role":"tool","content":"{\"success\":true,\"file_path\":\"/Users/davekinkead/Projects/son-of-ralph/agents/REVIEWER.md\"}","tool_call_id":"call_-7965096665784976247"},{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"file_path\":\"/Users/davekinkead/Projects/son-of-ralph/agents/RALPH.md\",\"old_string\":\"## Return Format\\n\\nUse standard promise tags for all returns.\\n\\n### SUCCESS Return Format\\n```\\nSUCCESS: \\n\\nSummary:\\n- Completed: [N] PRDs\\n- Failed: [N] PRDs\\n- Commits: [hash1, hash2, ...]\\n```\\n\\nExample:\\n```\\nSUCCESS: \\n\\nSummary:\\n- Completed: 2 PRDs\\n- Failed: 1 PRD\\n- Commits: bf36aac, 5cf3ec9\\n```\\n\\n### FAILURE Return Format\\n```\\nFAILURE: [specific error message]\\n```\\n\\nExamples:\\n```\\nFAILURE: No PRDs directory found at prds/\\nFAILURE: Invalid agent name 'NONEXISTENT'. Available agents: CODER, REVIEWER, RALPH, HAIKU\\nFAILURE: Git not initialized. Cannot commit changes\\n```\\n\\n### When to Return COMPLETE\\n- All PRDs have been processed (completed or failed status)\\n- No PRDs found in prds/ directory (but directory exists)\\n- All PRDs already completed or failed when starting\\n\\n### When to Return FAILURE\\n- prds/ directory doesn't exist\\n- Agent spawn fails (first iteration)\\n- Git commit fails (blocking operation)\\n- File operation fails (blocking operation)\\n\\nReturn format uses standard SUCCESS/FAILURE prefixes: \\\"SUCCESS: message\\\" or \\\"FAILURE: message\\\"\",\"new_string\":\"## Return Content\\n\\nOn SUCCESS: provide a summary including:\\n- Number of PRDs completed\\n- Number of PRDs failed\\n- Git commit hashes (if any)\\n\\nOn FAILURE: provide specific details for:\\n- No PRDs directory found\\n- Invalid agent name\\n- Agent initialization failures\\n- Git operation failures\\n- File operation failures\"}","name":"editfile"},"id":"call_-7965175452667606224","index":0,"type":"function"}]},{"role":"tool","content":"{\"success\":true,\"file_path\":\"/Users/davekinkead/Projects/son-of-ralph/agents/RALPH.md\"}","tool_call_id":"call_-7965175452667606224"},{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"command\":\"bundle exec rspec spec/ralph/agent_spec.rb\"}","name":"bash"},"id":"call_-7965110100443035778","index":0,"type":"function"}]},{"role":"tool","content":"{\"output\":\"/Users/davekinkead/Projects/son-of-ralph/lib/ralph/logger.rb:2: warning: logger was loaded from the standard library, but will no longer be part of the default gems starting from Ruby 3.5.0.\\nYou can add logger to your Gemfile or gemspec to silence this warning.\\n/Users/davekinkead/Projects/son-of-ralph/lib/ralph/tool.rb:6: warning: method redefined; discarding old description\\n\\nRandomized with seed 51568\\n\\nRalph::Agent\\n #max_iterations\\n uses custom max_iterations from agent frontmatter\\n uses default max_iterati