e a Haiku bot')\\n end\\n end\\n ```\\n\\nPlease implement all changes as specified in this PRD.\"}","name":"spawnagent"},"id":"call_-7965118759097245187","index":0,"type":"function"}]},{"role":"tool","content":"\"SUCCESS: Implemented centralized return format system in Agent class\\n\\nChanges made:\\n1. **Modified `lib/ralph/agent.rb`**:\\n - Added `default_system_prompt` private method that returns the standardized SUCCESS/FAILURE format instructions\\n - Modified `#call` method to append the default system prompt to instructions\\n\\n2. **Added tests in `spec/ralph/agent_spec.rb`**:\\n - Test verifying default system prompt is appended to instructions\\n - Test confirming original agent instructions are preserved\\n\\n3. **Updated agent markdown files** to focus on WHAT to include, not HOW to format:\\n - **CODER.md**: Changed from \\\"Return 'SUCCESS:'\\\" to \\\"On SUCCESS: provide a short summary\\\"\\n - **REVIEWER.md**: Removed \\\"Return Format\\\" section, added \\\"Return Content\\\" section\\n - **RALPH.md**: Removed detailed format examples, added \\\"Return Content\\\" section\\n - **HAIKU.md**: No changes (no return format instructions)\\n\\nAll 114 tests pass. The centralized return format system reduces duplication across agent.md files by automatically appending the standardized return format instructions to all agents.\"","tool_call_id":"call_-7965118759097245187"},{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"agent_name\":\"REVIEWER\",\"instructions\":\"# Final Implementation Plan\\n\\n## Overview\\nCreate a centralized return format system that appends default prompt instructions to all agents, reducing duplication in agent.md files.\\n\\n## Changes Required\\n\\n1. Modify `lib/ralph/agent.rb`:\\n\\n Add private method:\\n ```ruby\\n def default_system_prompt\\n <<~PROMPT\\n\\n Always return your response in this format:\\n - SUCCESS: {short summary} - when task is complete\\n - FAILURE: {detailed explanation} - when task cannot be completed\\n PROMPT\\n end\\n ```\\n\\n Modify `#call` method (line 22-23):\\n ```ruby\\n def call(prompt)\\n @logger.info(@id, \\\"Starting agent execution\\\")\\n @messages = []\\n @instructions += default_system_prompt # Add this line\\n\\n iteration = 0\\n ```\\n\\n5. Update agents/*.md to focus on WHAT to include in success and failure messages, not HOW to format them.\\n\\n6. Add tests in `spec/ralph/agent_spec.rb`:\\n ```ruby\\n describe '#call' do\\n it 'appends default system prompt to instructions' do\\n agent = Ralph::Agent.new('HAIKU', client: client)\\n expect(agent.instructions).to include('SUCCESS:')\\n expect(agent.instructions).to include('FAILURE:')\\n end\\n\\n it 'preserves original agent instructions' do\\n agent = Ralph::Agent.new('HAIKU', client: client)\\n expect(agent.instructions).to include('You are a Haiku bot')\\n end\\n end\\n ```\\n\\nPlease review the implementation and verify it meets all requirements in the PRD.\"}","name":"spawnagent"},"id":"call_-7965093745206992737","index":0,"type":"function"}]},{"role":"tool","content":"\"## FAILURE\\n\\n### Missing PRD Requirements\\n\\nThe implementation plan requires creating a default system prompt with this specific format:\\n\\n```ruby\\ndef default_system_prompt\\n <<~PROMPT\\n\\n Always return your response in this format:\\n - SUCCESS: {short summary} - when task is complete\\n - FAILURE: {detailed explanation} - when task cannot be completed\\n PROMPT\\nend\\n```\\n\\n**The specs only verify partial content:**\\n- Tests check that `'SUCCESS:'` and `'FAILURE:'` are present in instructions\\n- They do NOT verify the complete format including:\\n - The header \\\"Always return your response in this format:\\\"\\n - The bullet point format \\\"- SUCCESS: {short summary} - when task is complete\\\"\\n - The bullet point format \\\"- FAILURE: {detailed explanation} - when task cannot be completed\\\"\\n\\nThis is a significant gap because the PRD requires specific formatting, but the tests only check for keyword presence rather than format compliance.\\n\\n### Missing Edge Cases\\n\\nThe following edge cases are untested:\\n1. **Empty instructions**: What if an agent.md has no instructions content? Should the default prompt still be added?\\n2. **Nil instructions**: What if instructions are somehow nil during call?\\n3. **Multiple calls to #call**: Does the default prompt get appended repeatedly each time `#call` is invoked? (This could create duplicate prompts)\\n\\n### Missing Error Cases\\n\\nNo error conditions are tested, such as:\\n- What happens if the agent.md file is malformed?\\n- What if instructions cannot be read?\\n\\n### Recommendation\\n\\nAdd or modify tests to:\\n\\n1. Verify the exact format of the default system prompt:\\n```ruby\\nit 'includes the complete default system prompt format' do\\n expect(client).to receive(:chat).and_return(...)\\n agent.call('test')\\n expect(agent.instructions).to include('Always return your response in this format:')\\n expect(agent.instructions).to include('- SUCCESS: {short summary} - when task is complete')\\n expect(agent.instructions).to include('- FAILURE: {detailed explanation} - when task cannot be completed')\\nend\\n```\\n\\n2. Test edge cases (empty instructions, multiple calls):\\n```ruby\\nit 'appends default prompt even when original instructions are empty' do\\n # test scenario with empty instructions\\nend\\n\\nit 'does not duplicate default prompt on multiple calls' do\\n # test calling agent.call twice to ensure prompt isn't duplicated\\nend\\n```\\n\\nThe existing tests follow good testing practices (behavior-focused, proper RSpec structure, no implementation details), but they fail to adequately verify the complete PRD requirements.\"","tool_call_id":"call_-7965093745206992737"},{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"file_path\":\"prds/system-prompt-001.md\",\"old_string\":\"# Final Implementation Plan\",\"new_string\":\"## Feedback History\\n\\n### REVIEWER (Iteration 1): FAILURE\\n**Date:** 2025-06-17\\n\\n### Missing PRD Requirements\\n\\nThe implementation plan requires creating a default system prompt with this specific format:\\n\\n```ruby\\ndef default_system_prompt\\n <<~PROMPT\\n\\n Always return your response in this format:\\n - SUCCESS: {short summary} - when task is complete\\n - FAILURE: {detailed explanation} - when task cannot be completed\\n PROMPT\\nend\\n```\\n\\n**The specs only verify partial content:**\\n- Tests check that `'SUCCESS:'` and `'FAILURE:'` are present in instructions\\n- They do NOT verify the complete format including:\\n - The header \\\"Always return your response in this format:\\\"\\n - The bullet point format \\\"- SUCCESS: {short summary} - when task is complete\\\"\\n - The bullet point format \\\"- FAILURE: {detailed explanation} - when task cannot be completed\\\"\\n\\nThis is a significant gap because the PRD requires specific formatting, but the tests only check for keyword presence rather than format compliance.\\n\\n### Missing Edge Cases\\n\\nThe following edge cases are untested:\\n1. **Empty instructions**: What if an agent.md has no instructions content? Should the default prompt still be added?\\n2. **Nil instructions**: What if instructions are somehow nil during call?\\n3. **Multiple calls to #call**: Does the default prompt get appended repeatedly each time `#call` is invoked? (This could create duplicate prompts)\\n\\n### Missing Error Cases\\n\\nNo error conditions are tested, such as:\\n- What happens if the agent.md file is malformed?\\n- What if instructions cannot be read?\\n\\n### Recommendation\\n\\nAdd or modify tests to:\\n\\n1. Verify the exact format of the default system prompt:\\n```ruby\\nit 'includes the complete default system prompt format' do\\n expect(client).to receive(:chat).and_return(...)\\n agent.call('test')\\n expect(agent.instructions).to include('Always return your response in this format:')\\n expect(agent.instructions).to include('- SUCCESS: {short summary} - when task is complete')\\n expect(agent.instructions).to include('- FAILURE: {detailed explanation} - when task cannot be completed')\\nend\\n```\\n\\n2. Test edge cases (empty instructions, multiple calls):\\n```ruby\\nit 'appends default prompt even when original instructions are empty' do\\n # test scenario with empty instructions\\nend\\n\\nit 'does not duplicate default prompt on multiple calls' do\\n # test calling agent.call twice to ensure prompt isn't duplicated\\nend\\n```\\n\\nThe existing tests follow good testing practices (behavior-focused, proper RSpec structure, no implementation details), but they fail to adequately verify the complete PRD requirements.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# Final Implementation Plan\"}","name":"editfile"},"id":"call_-7965146006370738477","index":0,"type":"function"}]},{"role":"tool","content":"{\"success\":true,\"file_path\":\"prds/system-prompt-001.md\"}","tool_call_id":"call_-7965146006370738477"}],"tools":[{"type":"function","function":{"name":"bash","description":"Execute bash commands in the project directory","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"command":{"type":"string","description":"The bash command to execute"}},"required":[]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"readfile","description":"Read the contents of a file","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"file_path":{"type":"string","description":"The absolute path to the file to read"}},"required":[]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"writefile","description":"Write content to a file (overwrites existing content)","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"file_path":{"type":"string","description":"The absolute path to the file to write"},"content":{"type":"string","description":"The content to write to the file"}},"required":[]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"editfile","description":"Edit a file by replacing old_string with new_string","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"f